<title>JAPAN: Ontario launches 3.25% yen/dollar samurai--Nikko.</title>
<headline>Ontario launches 3.25% yen/dollar samurai--Nikko.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/dollar dual</p>
<p>currency samurai issue was announced by lead manager Nikko</p>
<p>Securities on Thursday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  Province of Ontario</p>
<p> AMT		 30 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    3.25 pct</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> MATURITY	  17 July 2001</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  17 July 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	July 8 to July 16</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AA-, Moody's Aa3</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Nikko Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi</p>
<p>NOTES: The exchange rate was fixed at $4,761.90 per 500,000 yen. -- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8584</p>
</text>
